IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cga-types`

-- Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 — GOAL 1: SCOPE.
--
--   "Is the acquirer a consumer; is the thing supplied goods or services
--    within the Act; was it supplied in trade under a contract made after the
--    Act began; and has the Act been validly contracted out of?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1993_91.txt — ss 2, 7B, 41,
-- 43, 43A, 56.

§ `Goal 1 — scope`

-- s 2 "consumer means a person who— (a) acquires from a supplier goods or
-- services of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic, or household
-- use or consumption; and (b) does not acquire the goods or services, or hold
-- himself or herself out as acquiring the goods or services, for the purpose
-- of— (i) resupplying them in trade; or (ii) consuming them in the course of
-- a process of production or manufacture; or (iii) in the case of goods,
-- repairing or treating in trade other goods or fixtures on land".
@ref s 2 consumer
@export Whether a person is a consumer under s 2 of the Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 (NZ): they acquire goods or services of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption, and not (nor hold themselves out as acquiring them) to resupply in trade, to consume in production or manufacture, or to repair or treat other goods or fixtures in trade. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN a IS AN Acquirer  @desc Whether the goods or services are of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use, and whether they were acquired (or held out as acquired) for resupply, production, or repair in trade
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a consumer` a IF
        a's `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic, or household use or consumption`
    AND NOT a's `acquired, or held out as acquired, to resupply in trade`
    AND NOT a's `acquired, or held out as acquired, to consume in production or manufacture`
    AND NOT a's `acquired, or held out as acquired, to repair or treat other goods or fixtures in trade`

-- s 2 consumer (b)(iii) "in the case of goods": the repair limb excludes only
-- acquirers of goods.
@ref s 2 consumer
GIVEN a IS AN Acquirer, t IS A `Thing supplied`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a consumer of` a t IF
        a's `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic, or household use or consumption`
    AND NOT a's `acquired, or held out as acquired, to resupply in trade`
    AND NOT a's `acquired, or held out as acquired, to consume in production or manufacture`
    AND NOT (    a's `acquired, or held out as acquired, to repair or treat other goods or fixtures in trade`
             AND NOT t EQUALS `services`)

-- s 2 "goods ... (c) ... does not include a whole building, or part of a
-- whole building, attached to land unless the building is a structure that
-- is easily removable and is not designed for residential accommodation".
-- s 7B(1): gas (other than non-reticulated gas) and electricity are not
-- goods, and their supply is not a service, save for s 7A.
@ref ss 2 goods, 7B
GIVEN t IS A `Thing supplied`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` t IF
    NOT t EQUALS `a building attached to land, of any other kind`

-- s 43(2) "parties to an agreement may include a provision ... that the
-- provisions of this Act will not apply ..., provided that— (a) the
-- agreement is in writing; and (b) the goods or services are ... supplied
-- and acquired in trade; and (c) all parties to the agreement— (i) are in
-- trade; and (ii) agree to contract out ...; and (d) it is fair and
-- reasonable that the parties are bound by the provision".
@ref s 43(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Contracting out clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` c IF
        c's `the agreement is in writing`
    AND c's `supplied and acquired in trade`
    AND c's `all parties are in trade`
    AND c's `all parties agree to contract out`
    AND c's `it is fair and reasonable that the parties are bound`

-- s 41 "(1) Nothing in this Act shall apply in any case where goods or
-- services are supplied otherwise than in trade. (2) Nothing in this Act
-- shall give any person a right of redress against a charitable organisation
-- in any case where goods or services are supplied by the charitable
-- organisation for the principal purpose of benefiting the person to whom
-- the supply is made." That bars redress only against the charity (the
-- supplier), not against a manufacturer; the goal applies it there. s 56 "This Act does not apply to any contract for the
-- supply of goods or services made before the commencement of this Act" (1
-- April 1994, s 1(2)). s 43(1) no contracting out except under s 43(2).
@ref ss 1(2), 2, 7B, 41, 43, 56
@export Whether the Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 (NZ) gives redress for a supply: the acquirer is a consumer (s 2); the thing is goods (not a fixed building other than an easily removable, non-residential structure), services, or gas or electricity from a retailer; it was supplied in trade (s 41(1)) and not by a charity for the principal purpose of benefiting the recipient (s 41(2)); the contract was made on or after 1 April 1994 (s 56); and the parties have not validly contracted out (s 43). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN a IS AN Acquirer  @desc The acquirer's purpose and the kind of goods or services
      s IS A Supply  @desc The thing supplied, whether in trade or by a charity, the date of the contract, and any contracting-out clause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act gives redress for the supply to` a `, supply` s IF
        `the Act applies to the supply to` a `, supply` s
    AND NOT s's `supplied by a charity for the principal purpose of benefiting the recipient`

-- The Act applies, before s 41(2): redress against a manufacturer survives a
-- charity's supply (s 41(2) protects only "a charitable organisation").
@ref ss 2, 41(1), 43, 56
GIVEN a IS AN Acquirer, s IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the supply to` a `, supply` s IF
        `is a consumer of` a (s's `thing supplied`)
    AND `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` (s's `thing supplied`)
    AND s's `supplied in trade`
    AND s's `contract made on` AT LEAST Date 1 4 1994
    AND CONSIDER s's `clause contracting out`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST k THEN NOT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` k

§§ `Courts and the Disputes Tribunal (s 47)`

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the High Court`
    `the District Court`
    `the Disputes Tribunal`

-- s 47 "(2) ... court of competent jurisdiction means— (a) the High Court:
-- (b) the District Court in any case where— (i) a claim ... does not exceed
-- $350,000 ... (4) The Disputes Tribunal shall have jurisdiction to hear and
-- determine any claim ... where the claim does not exceed $60,000."
@ref s 47
@export Which courts or tribunal may hear a claim for costs, damages or a refund under s 47 of the Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 (NZ): the High Court always; the District Court for claims up to $350,000; the Disputes Tribunal for claims up to $60,000. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN claim IS A NUMBER  @desc The amount claimed
GIVETH A LIST OF Forum
`the forums for a claim of` claim MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF claim AT MOST 60000  THEN LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`, `the Disputes Tribunal`
        IF claim AT MOST 350000 THEN LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`
        OTHERWISE LIST `the High Court`

§§ `Liability of assignees and creditors (s 46)`

-- s 46 "(1) The liability under this Act of an assignee of the rights of a
-- supplier ... shall not exceed the amount owing by the consumer under the
-- contract at the date of the assignment. (2) The liability ... of a
-- creditor who has lent money on the security of goods ... shall not exceed
-- the amount owing by the consumer at the date of the loan."
@ref s 46(1)-(2)
GIVEN claim IS A NUMBER, owing IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most an assignee or creditor is liable for, claim` claim `, owing at the date` owing MEANS
    min claim owing
